  "term": "respiratory depression",
  "definition": "Respiratory depression is a dangerous slowing and disruption of breathing, marked by reduced ventilation and rising carbon dioxide levels in the blood. In the context of opioid use, it can progress to irregular breathing and apnea, making it a major cause of death in overdose.",
